  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\nGodan verb ({打|う}ち{負|ま}かす → {打|う}ち{負|ま}かさない → {打|う}ち{負|ま}かして). Transitive: takes を to mark the defeated party.\n\nUSAGE:\nThe {打|う}ち〜 prefix adds emphasis and forcefulness, similar to English \"beat soundly\" or \"trounce.\" Stronger than {勝|か}つ (to win) and implies a more decisive victory.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {勝|か}つ: to win (neutral)\n- {負|ま}かす: to defeat (less emphatic)\n- {倒|たお}す: to defeat, to bring down (also emphatic)",
